Lunduke's Linux Kernel (lunduke-linux-kernel)
=============================================

Metapackage for linux-image-7.2.6-lunduke (ABI lcos22). Recommends matching
headers.

LCOS 0.8 ISOs shipped 7.2.6-lcos12 (that config stays frozen). lcos13
through lcos17 stay frozen. This metapackage is the lcos22
revision of the same 7.2.6-lunduke image name. On older LCOS releases
that still ship a Distro/Devuan kernel, install from the apt overlay,
reboot, and pick 7.2.6-lunduke in GRUB (or set it once).

  sudo apt update
  sudo apt install lunduke-linux-kernel

Apt overlay: https://lcos.lunduke.com/apt

lcos22: Realtek USB Wi-Fi rtw89 8852CU/8852BU/8851BU/8922AU and rtw88
8814AE (=m, LCOS#138) on lcos21.
lcos21: Intel VMD (CONFIG_VMD=m, NVMe behind Dell "RAID On") and PCIe
native hotplug (CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE=y) on lcos20.
lcos20: exFAT (CONFIG_EXFAT_FS=m, iocharset utf8, LCOS#131) on lcos19.
Userspace tools: exfatprogs.
lcos19: AMD GPU config audit (LCOS#115/#118).
lcos18: LUKS disk encryption (CONFIG_DM_CRYPT=m, CRYPTO_XTS/ESSIV/
AES_NI_INTEL=m, CRYPTO_USER_API_SKCIPHER/HASH=m, LCOS#123), UHID for
Bluetooth LE HID (CONFIG_UHID=m, LCOS#120), and RMI4 F11/F3A touchpad
functions (LCOS#121) on lcos17.
lcos17: SMB2/SMB3 client on lcos16 (CONFIG_CIFS=m, CONFIG_CIFS_XATTR=y,
LCOS#111). Mount with cifs-utils (mount -t cifs //nas/share /mnt -o ...).
SMB1 (CIFS_ALLOW_INSECURE_LEGACY), SMB Direct, and ksmbd stay off.
lcos16: LCOS 0.9 hardware gap pick-list on lcos15 (USB net/WWAN/serial,
AMD audio, Type-C, input, sensors, Wi-Fi/BT tail, Apple, Intel NPU,
VirtualBox guest, CONFIG_VFIO=m, CONFIG_VHOST_NET=m).
No Forced Rust. No firmware blob. No proprietary NVIDIA.
lcos12 through lcos17 stay frozen.
